| `doc style` | One checkable claim per sentence, naming the mechanism that enforces it. Keel-only records sit in one folder that one Copier exclusion leaves out, so a generated project never receives them. A shipped document cites only checks that run, and every shipped text source names no path under an unconditional exclusion under `docs/` except a test module with the module-level copier-absent skip guard (`tests/integration/test_doc_drift.py`), a compound report of a change (`now uses`, `no longer accepts`, `was renamed to`) in prose fails the same test, and a thought that opens with a bare change phrase is reported for review (`scripts/jobs/review_docs.py`). | `make check-docs`; `make test`; `make doc-review` | [`change_comments.phrases`](settings.md#configprojectjson) | The mechanical floor is gated; a bare change phrase, at an opener or in mid-sentence, and a count stated in prose are review's, and the compound-report scan reads one line at a time, so a report hard-wrapped across two lines passes. | [doc-style.md](../guides/doc-style.md) | always |
